      "question": "How to calculate retained earnings at the end of the period?",
      "type": "ai_overview",
      "text_blocks": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "snippet": "Retained earnings at the end of a period are calculated by adding the beginning retained earnings to the net income earned during the period and then subtracting any dividends paid out to shareholders. In simpler terms, it's the accumulated profits a company has kept over time.",
